<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pasłęka</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Passarge River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pasłęka, in German the Passarge, is a river of about 170 kilometres in the Warmian-Masurian region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> that flows north-west into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula-lagoon">Vistula Lagoon</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/braniewo">Braniewo</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it marked the boundary between the Baltic Prussian lands of Pogesania and Warmia, and it later formed part of the western border of the prince-bishopric of Warmia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pasleka.jpg" alt="Pasłęka" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: image/photo was taken by Wikipedia and Wikimedia Commons user Ludwig Schneider. I would appreciate being notified if ... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Braniewo_005.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
